    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f11a4cca-365c-5bbf-a722-c0d0bfdd7503",
      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=24 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-24 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-8.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-8)=-24.\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-24-(-8)=-16.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=-16$ and ${x}_{3}=-8$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(-16)-(-8)=24.\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=24-(16)-(8)=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=0$, ${x}_{2}=-16$, and ${x}_{3}=-8.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n⟨0,-16,-8⟩.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
